  "description": {
    "sub_id3": null,
    "sub_name": "遊戲與創意的跨域探索",
    "sub_ename": "AN INTERDISCIPLINARY EXPLORATION OF GAMES AND CREATIVITY",
    "describe_ch": "你不一定是人文社會學院的學生，但你每天都在使用語言、與人互動、感受情緒，也生活在由故事、文化與規則構成的世界中。人社院關心的，正是這些影響我們理解自我與他人的核心能力。本探索課程由中文、外文、人類學與戲劇四個領域教師跨域共授，專為外系學生設計，帶領學生以不同於傳統上課方式的途徑，認識人文社會學院的學習樣貌。\r\n課程拒絕枯燥理論，主張「遊戲是最高形式的學習」，從實際參與與體驗出發，結合文學故事的想像、人類學對儀式與文化的解析、戲劇的身體行動，以及語言與跨文化的實作，引導學生在無壓力的「玩」中打開五感。透過故事性圖像、影像敘事與互動式快閃活動，將抽象概念轉化為可感、可做、可共作的學習經驗。\r\n同時，課程導入社會情緒學習（SEL），在遊戲歷程中培養專注力、情緒管理與合作溝通能力，回應 Z 世代常見的注意力碎片化與社交焦慮問題。這不只是一門舒壓的課，更是一扇理解人文社會學院、重新認識世界與自己的入口。\r\n",
    "describe_eh": "You do not need to be a humanities student to join this course. Every day, you use language, interact with others, experience emotions, and live in a world shaped by stories, cultures, and social rules. This interdisciplinary exploration course, taught by faculty from Chinese Literature, Foreign Languages, Anthropology, and Theatre, invites students from all majors to experience how the humanities approach learning and understanding the world.\r\nRather than focusing on lectures or abstract theory, the course is built on the idea that play is the highest form of learning. Through hands-on activities, students explore literary storytelling, cultural rituals, embodied performance, and cross-cultural communication. Creative projects such as visual storytelling, video-making, and interactive flash mob activities help turn ideas into shared experiences.\r\nThe course also integrates Social and Emotional Learning (SEL), supporting focus, emotional awareness, collaboration, and communication. More than a stress-relief class, it offers international students a welcoming gateway to connect with others and rediscover learning through creativity and play.\r\n",
    "pre_subname": "",
    "pre_sub_id3": null,
    "pre_sub_ename": "",
    "pre_describe": null,
    "pre_describe_en": null,
    "scr_credit": 2.0
  },
